<title>UK: Zeneca registers new fungicide in US.</title>
<headline>Zeneca registers new fungicide in US.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Zeneca Group Plc said on Wednesday that the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency had registered its new fungicide, called Abound, for use on grapes, pecans, peanuts, peaches and bananas.</p>
<p>The EPA designated the fungicide as a &quot;reduced risk pesticide&quot; because it is less toxic and has a more &quot;favourable environmental profile&quot; than other registered fungicides, Zeneca said in a statement.</p>
</text>
